      "writtenOn": "2020-12-08T16:39:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re: just giving up, I think that\u0027s in the spirit of the spec\u0027s recommendation to Hard Reset, although I think that section is written with VBUS primarily in mind.\n\nHypothetically, if this happened after the cable had responded to a message, and we timed out during subsequent cable communication due to not sourcing VCONN, we would try to Soft Reset the cable, and we would eventually send a Hard Reset. (That\u0027s wrong. We have a bug open to implement Cable Reset.) I think the much more likely scenario is that this would happen immediately upon attach, so I\u0027m not super worried about that.\n\nOnce we have Cable Reset working, I think the end result of this happening at any point would be for us to just stop trying to talk to the cable.",
